After ascending a priest a few months ago, I decided to try
wizards.  I don't know how many characters I went through
until I learned how to properly identify B/U/C status...  in
fact, this game still had a few identify mistakes.

A magic lamp on the second or third dungeon level provided
+2 silver dragon scale mail.  A huge bones level that had the
corpses of two previous wizards provided a lot of cursed
rings and wands, but nothing really useful except a bag of
holding, once I managed to uncurse it, and magicbane...
As usual for me, I completed sokoban first, and got an
amulet of reflection (not really useful, given the silver
dragon scale mail), so it got stashed somewhere.  The mines
were quite easy- I converted the altar, and eventually
received Orcrist.  Mine's end was the gnome king's wine cellar,
with nothing interesting to note.

I'm still really bad at remembering to take notes on things...
I think the quest was on level 12, with the portal to Fort
Ludios one level down from that.  There was no big room in
this game.  I made it almost to medusa's island until I finally
reached level 13, at which point the potion of gain level
that I was carrying allowed me to head to the quest.  The
quest was very easy, as it always seems to be for me (the
wizard quest was MUCH easier than the priest one for me).

The one death that is mentioned in my end of game output
came from... drum roll please...  choking on a tin of spinach.
Someday I'll learn not to eat things that I don't have to
eat when I'm satiated...  this time I was wearing an amulet
of life saving however.  I figured at the time that since
I had completed the quest already and that I had a few good
pieces of equipment (scale mail, cloak of protection, speed
boots, magic marker) that I might just make it and be able
to talk about surviving such a silly death... good guess
this time.  :)

I had one other incident before the castle- it involved
sacrificing something insignificant (a troll maybe?  I
can't remember) on an altar to try to convert it.  It
converted me instead.  I'm still not sure why that happened.
It definitely wasn't a human or a unicorn that I sacrificed.
Fortunately, it happened after the quest, and right before
the castle, so it was only a minor inconvenience.

Things after the castle were fairly straightforward.  Since
I finally learned about named demons teleporting to the stairs,
it was much easier for me to dispatch them this time.  The
free wand of death was nice as well.  I'm still wondering why
Vlad is such a wimp- the guy died to ONE magic missle, and I
was only about level 16 at the time.

After getting the invocation artifacts and making my way
back up, I was thrown back somewhere around 10 times.  Rodney
appeared only about 3 times after our initial meeting, and
the wand of death that Orcus provided was quite helpful
each time, although it did miss once.  I didn't spend much
time sacrificing this game, so I never got crowned, thus
never receiving a spellbook of finger of death, and I guess
I completely forgot that I could just write it myself...

The planes were fairly easy- air elementals almost did me in,
but I started blowing wand of death charges left and right to
evacuate myself so I could head toward the portal.  On the
astral plane, I chose the left altar- it was the altar to 
my original chaotic god.  What suprised me was that the monsters
did NOT follow me into the temple, despite the fact that I
was no longer chaotic.  Not wanting to screw things up,
I went ahead and put on the helm of opposite alignment and
put myself back to chaotic (I figured that since Anhur had
been kind enough to provide for me in the early game, there
was no shame in handing him the amulet, since the lawful gods
really hadn't provided me with much of anything after my
accident...).

